id: pm-rl-irmn
title: Decoding stdin chunk by chunk corrupts a multi-byte character split across a chunk boundary
description: "readStdin decoded each binary chunk with Buffer.toString and joined the results. A stream splits on byte boundaries, not character boundaries, so a multi-byte UTF-8 sequence straddling two chunks decoded to two replacement characters, one on each side of the split. Piped NDJSON containing any non-ASCII text was silently corrupted, and a truncated trailing sequence was dropped rather than reported."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:cli","area:encoding","type:defect"
created_at: "2026-08-28T05:20:43.088Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T05:20:55.473Z"
deadline: "2026-08-29T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T05:20:55.459Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T05:20:55.459Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: A multi-byte character split across two chunks is reassembled exactly; a truncated trailing sequence is flushed as a replacement character rather than dropped; both assertions fail when the per-chunk decode is restored; the coverage gate still reports 100 percent.
resolution: "readStdin decodes binary chunks through a node:string_decoder StringDecoder and flushes the held tail with end(), so an incomplete sequence is carried to the next chunk instead of being decoded as garbage."
expected_result: "Piped NDJSON containing non-ASCII text arrives byte-for-byte identical regardless of where the producer flushed, and a truncated final sequence is reported as a replacement character."
actual_result: "Restoring the per-chunk decode fails only the boundary reassembly test; removing the end() flush fails only the truncated-tail test. Suite: 19 passed 0 failed. Gates: typecheck 0, lint 0, docstring 0 (17 files, 131 declarations), coverage 100/100/100 across 17 files."
