comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T05:20:43.088Z",claude,"Both new tests were proven to discriminate independently: restoring the per-chunk decode failed only the boundary reassembly test,and removing the decoder end() flush failed only the truncated-tail test."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T05:20:43.088Z",claude,"Demonstrated outside the repo: decoding the two halves of the two-byte sequence for e-acute separately yields two replacement characters,while concatenating the bytes first yields the character."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T05:20:43.088Z",claude,Treat every chunk boundary in a byte stream as arbitrary. Decoding per chunk makes the output depend on how the producer happened to flush.
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,readStdin decodes binary chunks through a StringDecoder and flushes the tail with end()
  test/index.test.ts,project,boundary reassembly and truncated-tail flush tests
